      "source": [
        "Throughout this workshop, we work with the `USSteamCo` data file, this is available in the `aicpa` package. The data file is used in the AICPA Guide to Audit Analytics, Exhibit B-3.\n",
        "The audit task is to use production and weather-related information to explain revenue and later assess whether expected revenue is consistent with the observed data. The key variables are `revenue` (the dependent variable, expressed in US dollars), `production` (the steam production, in thousands of pounds), and `coolDD` and `heatDD` (the cooling and heating degree days, which count the days on which outside air temperatures were higher or lower than a specified base temperature). The dummy variable `summer` is added to the dataset in Exercise 5.3. Start by checking what variables are available and what one monthly record looks like.\n",
        "The `head` function shows the values of the variables (columns) in the first few observations (rows) from the dataset.\n"
      ]
